// The operator list restricts which operators fold: only `+` is listed. So
// `(+ 1 2)` folds to `3` and is baked into the abstraction, but `(* 4 5)` does
// NOT fold (its operator is excluded) and therefore does not unify with the
// literal `20` the other programs write — it has to be passed as an argument.
constant_folding: !integers (params (ops (+)))
